2204
00:03:12,967 --> 00:03:15,507
This is World Smile Land.

2205
00:03:15,507 --> 00:03:21,597
It's an amusement city that exists
 to give our patrons an eternal smile.

2206
00:03:21,597 --> 00:03:22,557
Yep.

2207
00:03:22,557 --> 00:03:27,567
The whole city is a wonderful amusement park.

2208
00:03:27,567 --> 00:03:34,487
Which means the people of this
 city can play and laugh year-round.

2209
00:03:34,487 --> 00:03:39,037
Of course, to make sure they keep smiling,

2210
00:03:39,037 --> 00:03:43,417
we come out with new animals and characters all the time.

2211
00:03:43,417 --> 00:03:47,497
Also, attractions and cast members that people get bored with

2212
00:03:47,497 --> 00:03:50,127
go bye-bye in a flash!

2213
00:03:50,547 --> 00:03:52,047
And this place...

2214
00:03:52,047 --> 00:03:54,757
Is where they get dumped!

2215
00:04:08,607 --> 00:04:10,357
That was a close call.

2216
00:04:10,937 --> 00:04:13,027
By the way, Miss, what's your name?

2217
00:04:13,027 --> 00:04:15,317
Why did you come here?

2218
00:04:15,317 --> 00:04:20,747
I was traveling with Vince and Re-l on the rabbit, but...

2219
00:04:20,747 --> 00:04:22,287
Vince?

2220
00:04:22,287 --> 00:04:23,657
Re-l?

2221
00:04:24,287 --> 00:04:25,457
You know them?

2222
00:04:25,457 --> 00:04:27,377
Not at all.

2223
00:04:27,377 --> 00:04:31,207
We're <i>NakaMa</i> who get along great!

2224
00:04:34,127 --> 00:04:37,387
I wonder if I got thrown away too.

2225
00:04:38,387 --> 00:04:40,467
I'm in trouble...

2226
00:04:40,467 --> 00:04:42,227
Trouble, trouble...

2227
00:04:42,227 --> 00:04:44,227
Mm, trouble...

2228
00:04:44,227 --> 00:04:45,437
I know!

2229
00:04:44,687 --> 00:04:46,977
When in trouble, ask!

2230
00:04:46,977 --> 00:04:48,477
All right!

2231
00:04:48,477 --> 00:04:52,067
We are in trouble right now too, actually.

2232
00:04:52,067 --> 00:04:55,607
It's so great that we're all in trouble at the same time!

2233
00:04:55,907 --> 00:04:57,567
What are we going to ask?

2234
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:59,867
That's obvious!

2235
00:04:59,867 --> 00:05:03,747
We're going to ask the creator of our world's smiles:

2236
00:05:03,747 --> 00:05:07,287
Will B. Good!

2237
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:13,087
You're better off not ad-libbing like that.

2238
00:05:14,127 --> 00:05:16,877
There's no time left for that, you know.

2239
00:05:17,257 --> 00:05:19,217
Oh, here's the mole.

2240
00:05:19,217 --> 00:05:21,347
Oh, here's the spy.

2241
00:05:22,057 --> 00:05:23,097
Ignoring me, are you?

2242
00:05:23,097 --> 00:05:27,397
<u>Note:</u> He's trying to make a pun from "mushi", which can means "bug" or "to ignore".

2243
00:05:23,097 --> 00:05:24,637
Oh, just 'cause I'm a bug...

2244
00:05:24,637 --> 00:05:26,017
Hey, listen to me!

2245
00:05:26,017 --> 00:05:27,057
Who're you?

2246
00:05:27,057 --> 00:05:29,977
Oops, this is the real reason I'm here.

2247
00:05:29,977 --> 00:05:31,267
Miss,

2248
00:05:31,267 --> 00:05:35,147
if you stick with these guys, you're not going to get anywhere.

2249
00:05:35,147 --> 00:05:37,697
Jeez, I've been looking all over for you.

2250
00:05:37,697 --> 00:05:40,407
I had no idea you'd wandered into a place like this.

2251
00:05:40,407 --> 00:05:43,737
<u>Note:</u> His name is a pun on the word for cricket (koorogi).

2252
00:05:40,697 --> 00:05:42,487
I'm Rogi the cricket.

2253
00:05:42,487 --> 00:05:43,737
Well, nice to meetcha.

2254
00:05:43,737 --> 00:05:46,907
I'm looking for Vince and Re-l.

2255
00:05:46,907 --> 00:05:48,747
That's what I thought!

2256
00:05:48,747 --> 00:05:49,577
You know them?

2257
00:05:49,577 --> 00:05:51,037
Of course!

2258
00:05:51,037 --> 00:05:55,167
You'll find out where they are if you come with me to Will B. Good.

2259
00:05:55,167 --> 00:05:56,337
Alrighty.

2260
00:05:56,337 --> 00:05:57,587
Let's go!

2261
00:05:58,127 --> 00:05:59,177
But...

2262
00:05:59,177 --> 00:06:01,137
Um... Like this...

2263
00:06:01,137 --> 00:06:02,257
Uhh...

2264
00:06:02,257 --> 00:06:07,057
Their... roles are over.

2265
00:06:08,977 --> 00:06:10,977
Never mind the nitty-gritty details!

2266
00:06:11,397 --> 00:06:15,567
<u>Note:</u> This refers to Akutagawa Ryuunosuke's famous work, "The Spider's Thread",
 in which Buddha lowers a spider's thread into hell to save a sinner.

2267
00:06:11,397 --> 00:06:13,567
This is like spider's thread!

2268
00:06:15,857 --> 00:06:17,237
Hold on!

2269
00:06:56,397 --> 00:06:58,607
We lost the postcards, didn't we.

2270
00:06:58,607 --> 00:07:00,357
That's fine.

2271
00:07:00,357 --> 00:07:03,567
We've discovered that just asking isn't good enough.

2272
00:07:03,567 --> 00:07:05,577
So we're going to take action.

2273
00:07:05,577 --> 00:07:08,827
Actually, why are you guys coming with us?

2274
00:07:08,827 --> 00:07:12,287
We're going to Will B. Good.

2275
00:07:12,287 --> 00:07:13,827
Why?

2276
00:07:13,827 --> 00:07:15,997
To ask him why we were born.

2277
00:07:15,997 --> 00:07:19,127
Good would know, since he created us.

2278
00:07:19,127 --> 00:07:20,627
How idiotic.

2279
00:07:20,627 --> 00:07:23,507
You've changed your reason too.

2280
00:07:23,507 --> 00:07:25,637
But I guess you're gonna ignore me again anyway.

2281
00:07:25,637 --> 00:07:28,017
I'm sure there's a reason why we were born.

2282
00:07:28,017 --> 00:07:30,637
He has to tell us what it is.

2283
00:07:30,637 --> 00:07:32,267
A reason...

2284
00:07:33,397 --> 00:07:34,647
In any case,

2285
00:07:35,107 --> 00:07:38,437
you guys aren't a part of this deal.

2286
00:07:38,437 --> 00:07:40,147
Go home already.

2287
00:07:40,147 --> 00:07:41,897
We want to go too!

2288
00:07:41,897 --> 00:07:43,157
Want to!

2289
00:07:43,157 --> 00:07:46,157
Please take Arl and Pul too. Please?

2290
00:07:48,407 --> 00:07:51,247
That's why we should've left them behind.

2291
00:07:51,957 --> 00:07:53,457
I know.

2292
00:07:53,457 --> 00:07:55,077
Um...

2293
00:07:55,077 --> 00:07:58,127
I'm not trying to ask anything in return for taking them, but...

2294
00:07:58,127 --> 00:08:00,917
can you tell me one thing?

2295
00:08:00,917 --> 00:08:01,967
What?

2296
00:08:01,967 --> 00:08:03,297
Um...

2297
00:08:03,297 --> 00:08:05,887
What kind of person is this Mr. Vince?

2298
00:08:05,887 --> 00:08:07,557
He's nice to me.

2299
00:08:07,557 --> 00:08:09,217
So I love him.

2300
00:08:09,217 --> 00:08:12,177
And since Vince loves Re-l,

2301
00:08:12,177 --> 00:08:14,057
I love Re-l too.

2302
00:08:15,307 --> 00:08:18,567
Not that sort of thing... more like Mr. Vince's...

2303
00:08:18,567 --> 00:08:20,817
special traits?

2304
00:08:20,187 --> 00:08:21,527
Mm...

2305
00:08:21,527 --> 00:08:24,567
He's always being a wimp,

2306
00:08:25,487 --> 00:08:29,197
but sometimes he'll change in a flash and get big and strong!

2307
00:08:29,197 --> 00:08:30,747
Just as I thought.

2308
00:08:31,617 --> 00:08:34,707
And what is his Achilles' heel?

2309
00:08:36,077 --> 00:08:37,247
Hey!

2310
00:08:37,247 --> 00:08:38,207
Pino!

2311
00:08:38,207 --> 00:08:39,797
This way, this way!

2312
00:08:39,797 --> 00:08:41,337
Come take a look!

2313
00:08:43,507 --> 00:08:44,377
Dammit.

2314
00:08:44,377 --> 00:08:46,637
There's so little time left.

2315
00:09:04,737 --> 00:09:06,447
Super surprised!

2316
00:09:06,447 --> 00:09:07,817
Weren't you surprised?

2317
00:09:07,817 --> 00:09:09,617
It's good, Guest.

2318
00:09:09,617 --> 00:09:11,077
Doesn't it seem fun?

2319
00:09:11,077 --> 00:09:12,867
Good for you, Guest!

2320
00:09:12,867 --> 00:09:14,367
Totally!

2321
00:09:14,367 --> 00:09:16,367
Good, isn't it, Guests.

2322
00:09:16,367 --> 00:09:20,747
We're all <i>NakaMa</i> who get along great!

2323
00:09:21,297 --> 00:09:22,047
Geez.

2324
00:09:22,047 --> 00:09:25,877
Forget that. We need to go to Good quick...

2325
00:09:26,757 --> 00:09:29,757
Hey! You can't go outside!

2326
00:09:36,267 --> 00:09:37,347
So exciting!

2327
00:09:37,347 --> 00:09:38,097
Isn't it?

2328
00:09:38,097 --> 00:09:39,437
Right, right, right!

2329
00:09:40,607 --> 00:09:43,277
This is posted all over.

2330
00:09:43,277 --> 00:09:47,527
This is a notice that the end of everyone's world is near.

2331
00:09:47,527 --> 00:09:50,527
Well, not that it has anything to do with us.

2332
00:09:50,527 --> 00:09:51,827
Idiot!

2333
00:09:51,827 --> 00:09:55,497
You and I are all included in the "everyone"!

2334
00:09:55,497 --> 00:09:57,367
It's the end of the world!

2335
00:09:57,367 --> 00:09:59,377
Armageddon's coming soon!

2336
00:09:59,377 --> 00:10:01,537
Uh, are you ignoring me again?

2337
00:10:01,537 --> 00:10:06,547
I heard that it's a story that Good's
 been writing while cooped up in his room.

2338
00:10:06,547 --> 00:10:09,717
Though it's not coming along at all.

2339
00:10:10,387 --> 00:10:11,297
Jeez.

2340
00:10:11,297 --> 00:10:12,927
Who cares?

2341
00:10:12,927 --> 00:10:15,677
Let's just go to Will...

2342
00:10:15,677 --> 00:10:16,677
I'm begging you guys.

2343
00:10:16,977 --> 00:10:18,637
You there.

2344
00:10:18,637 --> 00:10:20,687
Do all of you have a pass?

2345
00:10:20,687 --> 00:10:21,937
No.

2346
00:10:21,937 --> 00:10:23,147
Um...

2347
00:10:23,687 --> 00:10:26,187
Well, you can't ride for free!

2348
00:10:27,857 --> 00:10:29,947
Told ya.

2349
00:10:30,657 --> 00:10:31,447
Pino!

2350
00:10:31,447 --> 00:10:32,197
Run!

2351
00:10:35,157 --> 00:10:36,117
Get her!

2352
00:10:36,117 --> 00:10:37,287
Wait, stop!

2353
00:10:38,997 --> 00:10:41,377
Fun!

2354
00:10:42,497 --> 00:10:43,997
Give up!

2355
00:10:44,377 --> 00:10:46,257
Hey, look. That girl...

2356
00:10:47,627 --> 00:10:48,377
Get her-

2357
00:10:50,757 --> 00:10:52,387
She's great.

2358
00:10:52,387 --> 00:10:53,887
She's smiling...

2359
00:10:53,887 --> 00:10:55,757
but so naturally...

2360
00:10:59,687 --> 00:11:02,187
I've never seen anyone smile like that.

2361
00:11:07,437 --> 00:11:08,487
Not to mention...

2362
00:11:08,487 --> 00:11:09,487
Yeah.

2363
00:11:09,487 --> 00:11:11,157
She's not faking it.

2364
00:11:12,617 --> 00:11:13,947
Pino...

2365
00:11:14,737 --> 00:11:16,197
It stops here!

2366
00:11:16,787 --> 00:11:17,487
Wha?

2367
00:11:17,947 --> 00:11:18,747
Wha?

2368
00:11:18,747 --> 00:11:20,207
Whaaa?

2369
00:11:20,497 --> 00:11:21,577
Pino!

2370
00:11:32,007 --> 00:11:32,837
No!

2371
00:11:32,837 --> 00:11:35,467
I don't need ad-libs in <i>my</i> world!

2372
00:11:49,437 --> 00:11:52,027
Pino was great.

2373
00:11:52,027 --> 00:11:55,027
Pino looked like she was having so much fun.

2374
00:11:55,317 --> 00:11:57,987
It was really fun.

2375
00:11:57,987 --> 00:12:03,287
I remember Papa taking me to a mall a long time ago.

2376
00:12:03,617 --> 00:12:06,537
Wow, you have a father even though you're a machine?

2377
00:12:06,537 --> 00:12:09,297
But we haven't been together for a long time.

2378
00:12:09,297 --> 00:12:10,877
That's so sad.

2379
00:12:10,877 --> 00:12:12,797
Do you want to see your father again?

2380
00:12:14,297 --> 00:12:16,297
No, I'm okay.

2381
00:12:16,297 --> 00:12:17,677
Why?

2382
00:12:17,677 --> 00:12:19,347
He's still your father, right?

2383
00:12:19,347 --> 00:12:22,307
But I'm with important <i>NakaMa</i> now.

2384
00:12:22,307 --> 00:12:24,727
So that's Vince...

2385
00:12:24,727 --> 00:12:26,107
And Re-l.

2386
00:12:26,107 --> 00:12:27,557
I hope we'll get to meet them.

2387
00:12:28,017 --> 00:12:28,857
Yeah.

2388
00:12:29,727 --> 00:12:33,067
What are you <i>NakaMa</i> going to do after meeting Good?

2389
00:12:33,067 --> 00:12:37,067
Hmm, well, the attraction we were living in is gone.

2390
00:12:37,067 --> 00:12:40,577
Oh, then I want to be a guest next!

2391
00:12:40,577 --> 00:12:44,077
Oh! I just thought of that too!

2392
00:12:44,077 --> 00:12:47,207
Jeez, your reason changed again.

2393
00:12:47,207 --> 00:12:49,087
I bet you're going to ignore me again too.

2394
00:12:49,377 --> 00:12:50,587
A guest?

2395
00:12:50,587 --> 00:12:52,127
If that happens...

2396
00:12:52,457 --> 00:12:55,087
We can smile forever.

2397
00:12:58,097 --> 00:13:02,097
Do you understand the trouble you're in?!

2398
00:13:07,977 --> 00:13:11,727
<u>Note:</u> The name is a pun on the word for a dog's bark (wan).

2399
00:13:07,977 --> 00:13:10,727
Here it is, Police Detective Wan.

2400
00:13:12,027 --> 00:13:13,817
Uh, let's see...

2401
00:13:13,817 --> 00:13:16,737
First, the small one over there.

2402
00:13:16,737 --> 00:13:18,067
Rogi, eh.

2403
00:13:18,067 --> 00:13:20,737
An autoreiv for scouting and surveillance.

2404
00:13:20,737 --> 00:13:23,867
And the duo over there, Arl and Pul...

2405
00:13:23,867 --> 00:13:29,917
<u>Note:</u> The Commedia dell'arte was a popular form of improv theater that began in
          the 16th century and featured characters such as Arlecchino and Pulcinella.

2406
00:13:23,867 --> 00:13:29,207
You're both entertainment-type autoreivs
 and cast members of Commedia dell'arte.

2407
00:13:29,917 --> 00:13:31,127
Here.

2408
00:13:32,087 --> 00:13:34,967
Commedia dell'arte was just shut down!

2409
00:13:34,967 --> 00:13:38,387
Then you should've been sent off to the trash bin already!

2410
00:13:39,427 --> 00:13:42,927
And the biggest problem, you,

2411
00:13:42,927 --> 00:13:44,677
aren't in any of our records, but...

2412
00:13:44,677 --> 00:13:45,637
I'm Pino.

2413
00:13:46,097 --> 00:13:47,057
Who are you?

2414
00:13:47,057 --> 00:13:48,437
I'm me!

2415
00:13:48,727 --> 00:13:50,607
Th-That's...

2416
00:13:50,607 --> 00:13:52,897
A-A natural smile!

2417
00:13:52,897 --> 00:13:56,447
<u>Note:</u> The name is a pun on the word for a cat's meow (nyaa).

2418
00:13:52,897 --> 00:13:55,527
C-C-Calm down, Officer Nyarrl.

2419
00:13:55,527 --> 00:13:56,447
But!

2420
00:13:56,737 --> 00:13:59,947
Th-That's a mighty natural smile you've got there.

2421
00:13:59,947 --> 00:14:01,617
A new function, right?

2422
00:14:01,617 --> 00:14:06,827
I got a soul after I met <i>NakaMa</i> like Vince and Re-l.

2423
00:14:07,207 --> 00:14:10,667
So when I'm having fun, I smile.

2424
00:14:16,087 --> 00:14:18,217
Smile for me!

2425
00:14:18,217 --> 00:14:20,427
You're dazzling!

2426
00:14:21,257 --> 00:14:22,177
Ugh!

2427
00:14:22,177 --> 00:14:25,807
There's no time for this!

2428
00:14:27,477 --> 00:14:29,597
Listen up, everyone!

2429
00:14:29,597 --> 00:14:34,227
You're stuck in the exposition stage in
 the plot, and the story's going nowhere!

2430
00:14:34,227 --> 00:14:35,357
Forget it.

2431
00:14:35,357 --> 00:14:38,607
We're skipping the climax and jumping straight to the conclusion!

2432
00:14:43,277 --> 00:14:44,617
What?

2433
00:14:48,207 --> 00:14:49,787
Welcome.

2434
00:14:50,327 --> 00:14:53,037
Welcome to <i>my</i> world, World Smile Land.

2435
00:14:53,957 --> 00:14:55,627
Will B. Good!

2436
00:14:55,627 --> 00:14:57,627
Our creator!

2437
00:14:57,627 --> 00:15:01,047
Hi, my name is Will B. Good.

2438
00:15:01,547 --> 00:15:07,267
I created this to be a place where everyone can keep smiling.

2439
00:15:07,847 --> 00:15:12,857
But you know, that's actually harder than it looks.

2440
00:15:13,477 --> 00:15:17,607
Everyone can smile for a short while.

2441
00:15:17,607 --> 00:15:23,117
But the really hard part is to keep everyone smiling.

2442
00:15:23,777 --> 00:15:25,907
And do you know what?

2443
00:15:25,907 --> 00:15:29,327
Sometimes people laugh even when

2444
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:33,997
they've been scared witless or have cried their eyes out.

2445
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:38,047
To make perfect smiles,

2446
00:15:38,047 --> 00:15:40,547
you need tight control on things.

2447
00:15:41,297 --> 00:15:45,507
And that's why I made Smile Land.

2448
00:15:46,007 --> 00:15:47,717
Perfect smiles...

2449
00:15:47,717 --> 00:15:49,977
Smiles that should be made and protected...

2450
00:15:49,977 --> 00:15:52,807
Wonderful smiles that make the world happy...

2451
00:15:53,307 --> 00:15:55,767
Smiles that let people forget reality

2452
00:15:55,767 --> 00:15:59,937
and the terror that awaits until the last possible moment.

2453
00:15:59,937 --> 00:16:00,937
Yes...

2454
00:16:01,447 --> 00:16:02,987
The people of this city

2455
00:16:02,987 --> 00:16:07,027
play here from the day they're born until the day they die.

2456
00:16:07,527 --> 00:16:13,917
And they can meet the world's end, ignorant and happy.

2457
00:16:14,747 --> 00:16:16,377
Isn't that great?

2458
00:16:17,207 --> 00:16:18,797
Great, great!

2459
00:16:18,797 --> 00:16:20,047
Good, good.

2460
00:16:20,047 --> 00:16:20,837
Pino,

2461
00:16:21,337 --> 00:16:24,377
you want to see Vince and Re-l, don't you.

2462
00:16:24,377 --> 00:16:25,467
You know them?

2463
00:16:25,467 --> 00:16:26,797
Of course.

2464
00:16:26,797 --> 00:16:28,637
I know everything.

2465
00:16:28,637 --> 00:16:30,807
After all, I'm the creator.

2466
00:16:31,267 --> 00:16:35,017
But before that, can you tell me a tiny little something?

2467
00:16:35,017 --> 00:16:39,477
What is Vincent's - no, Ergo PROXY's - weakness?

2468
00:16:40,317 --> 00:16:41,397
Weird.

2469
00:16:41,857 --> 00:16:44,197
You said you know everything.

2470
00:16:44,777 --> 00:16:48,157
Can't you whisper it to me, like you would a secret?

2471
00:16:48,617 --> 00:16:50,117
I don't know.

2472
00:16:50,117 --> 00:16:52,907
Then do you not want to see them?

2473
00:16:52,907 --> 00:16:54,077
I do.

2474
00:16:54,077 --> 00:16:56,627
Then please tell me.

2475
00:16:57,077 --> 00:16:58,627
But I really don't know.

2476
00:16:58,627 --> 00:17:00,997
Then do you know anything?

2477
00:17:00,997 --> 00:17:05,007
Like, what he considers a treasure...

2478
00:17:05,007 --> 00:17:07,297
Come now... Remember...

2479
00:17:07,297 --> 00:17:09,257
G-Good...

2480
00:17:09,717 --> 00:17:11,217
A treasure...

2481
00:17:11,217 --> 00:17:12,267
to Vince...

2482
00:17:19,647 --> 00:17:20,857
I don't know!

2483
00:17:26,447 --> 00:17:27,607
Are you telling the truth?

2484
00:17:27,607 --> 00:17:29,117
It's true!

2485
00:17:29,117 --> 00:17:30,487
I see.

2486
00:17:30,487 --> 00:17:32,037
That's too bad.

2487
00:17:32,577 --> 00:17:36,537
Because if you had Vince's treasure right now...

2488
00:17:37,037 --> 00:17:40,247
I could grant you any wish...

2489
00:17:40,247 --> 00:17:41,917
You're lying.

2490
00:17:43,007 --> 00:17:44,837
Good, good...

2491
00:17:44,837 --> 00:17:47,837
Now then, look behind you.

2492
00:17:49,387 --> 00:17:50,257
Who are you?

2493
00:17:50,257 --> 00:17:51,847
What are you saying?

2494
00:17:51,847 --> 00:17:53,307
It's us.

2495
00:17:53,307 --> 00:17:54,927
Arl and Pul.

2496
00:17:54,927 --> 00:17:56,847
We asked him to make us into visitors.

2497
00:17:58,937 --> 00:18:01,897
I granted their wish.

2498
00:18:01,897 --> 00:18:03,437
You get it now, don't you?

2499
00:18:03,437 --> 00:18:06,817
I'll grant your wish next, Pino.

2500
00:18:07,277 --> 00:18:09,527
So, come...

2501
00:18:11,157 --> 00:18:14,867
Believe in me, the creator of this paradise of smiles...

2502
00:18:16,157 --> 00:18:17,157
Come...

2503
00:18:21,917 --> 00:18:25,377
Aren't those smiles kind of fake?

2504
00:18:26,717 --> 00:18:27,717
What?

2505
00:18:28,127 --> 00:18:31,217
Pino's smiles were so natural!

2506
00:18:31,217 --> 00:18:33,717
Our smiles are... sort of superficial...

2507
00:18:34,097 --> 00:18:36,217
Or shallow...

2508
00:18:36,217 --> 00:18:38,227
They don't have any substance.

2509
00:18:38,517 --> 00:18:39,767
Fake!

2510
00:18:39,767 --> 00:18:42,647
They're totally different from Pino's smiles.

2511
00:18:45,227 --> 00:18:46,857
Shut up!

2512
00:18:46,857 --> 00:18:48,317
How can <i>you</i>,

2513
00:18:48,317 --> 00:18:52,867
characters created by <i>me</i>, criticize <i>me</i>?

2514
00:18:52,867 --> 00:18:54,237
You're kidding me!

2515
00:18:54,657 --> 00:18:58,957
You guys will do as I say!

2516
00:18:59,747 --> 00:19:03,247
Getting in my way with your stupid ad-libs...!

2517
00:19:03,537 --> 00:19:06,587
Besides, what's all this about
 wanting to know the reason you were born?

2518
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:09,007
As if something like that exists!

2519
00:19:09,007 --> 00:19:12,637
You're all meaningless defects!

2520
00:19:12,637 --> 00:19:16,927
Geez! You worthless scum!

2521
00:19:19,307 --> 00:19:20,267
What?

2522
00:19:39,077 --> 00:19:40,787
So fun!

2523
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:47,797
W-Wait, please.

2524
00:19:47,797 --> 00:19:50,217
There's no time... left...

2525
00:19:50,217 --> 00:19:51,337
There's no time... left...

2526
00:19:52,087 --> 00:19:53,337
Please, Pino.

2527
00:19:53,337 --> 00:19:56,807
Please tell Vince and Re-l not to come here.

2528
00:19:58,097 --> 00:19:59,347
Listen.

2529
00:19:59,347 --> 00:20:01,807
Vince will come here soon.

2530
00:20:02,387 --> 00:20:04,437
When PROXIES meet...

2531
00:20:04,937 --> 00:20:07,607
He and I will have to fight.

2532
00:20:08,147 --> 00:20:09,647
Really?

2533
00:20:09,647 --> 00:20:10,567
Yes.

2534
00:20:11,187 --> 00:20:12,527
And if that happens...

2535
00:20:12,987 --> 00:20:15,277
this place won't stay peaceful anymore.

2536
00:20:16,117 --> 00:20:18,827
Will... everyone die?

2537
00:20:19,117 --> 00:20:20,327
Yes...

2538
00:20:20,327 --> 00:20:23,827
That's why I interfered with your dreams

2539
00:20:23,827 --> 00:20:26,247
and tried to find out what Vince's weakness was from you.

2540
00:20:26,247 --> 00:20:28,587
But that failed.

2541
00:20:29,087 --> 00:20:31,877
Is this... a dream?

2542
00:20:32,377 --> 00:20:35,137
It's a dream... and yet not a dream.

2543
00:20:35,887 --> 00:20:37,177
Really?

2544
00:20:37,177 --> 00:20:39,467
Aren't you messing with us again?

2545
00:20:39,467 --> 00:20:40,427
No!

2546
00:20:40,427 --> 00:20:41,807
It's true!

2547
00:20:41,807 --> 00:20:43,307
Please believe me.

2548
00:20:43,307 --> 00:20:46,477
The world will come to an end soon anyway.

2549
00:20:46,477 --> 00:20:48,107
That's just fate.

2550
00:20:48,437 --> 00:20:49,317
But...

2551
00:20:49,817 --> 00:20:51,527
until then...

2552
00:20:52,317 --> 00:20:55,107
I want to spend the time quietly here, smiling.

2553
00:20:56,157 --> 00:20:58,447
I don't want to fight anymore.

2554
00:20:59,327 --> 00:21:00,117
Pino,

2555
00:21:00,117 --> 00:21:02,117
we're asking you too.

2556
00:21:02,117 --> 00:21:05,327
We want to keep smiling too.

2557
00:21:05,327 --> 00:21:09,287
Because you taught us what a natural smile is, so...

2558
00:21:10,797 --> 00:21:12,257
<i>NakaMa</i>...

2559
00:21:14,547 --> 00:21:16,797
I can hear the heartbeat of beginning.

2560
00:21:18,087 --> 00:21:19,297
Soon...

2561
00:21:32,857 --> 00:21:33,857
Huh?

2562
00:21:47,997 --> 00:21:49,247
Gone...

2563
00:21:49,247 --> 00:21:50,247
They're gone!

2564
00:21:50,747 --> 00:21:52,667
Maybe I did give them to him...

2565
00:21:54,707 --> 00:21:56,007
Vince!

2566
00:21:58,547 --> 00:22:00,387
Are you done charging up?

2567
00:22:00,677 --> 00:22:04,217
Um, Vince, can you bend down a little?

2568
00:22:04,217 --> 00:22:05,177
What is it?

2569
00:22:07,267 --> 00:22:08,437
You have it!

2570
00:22:08,727 --> 00:22:10,647
Are you still half asleep?

2571
00:22:10,647 --> 00:22:14,147
Look, we're starting to see lights up ahead.

2572
00:22:14,147 --> 00:22:17,397
There may be a city.

2573
00:22:19,107 --> 00:22:21,697
It'll be nice if we can restock some of our supplies,

2574
00:22:21,697 --> 00:22:23,197
but getting some rest will be nice enough.

2575
00:22:23,197 --> 00:22:24,487
City...?

2576
00:22:24,997 --> 00:22:26,287
Could it be...

2577
00:22:38,217 --> 00:22:39,087
No!

2578
00:22:39,087 --> 00:22:40,507
We mustn't go there!

2579
00:22:40,507 --> 00:22:41,887
Did you fry a circuit?

2580
00:22:41,887 --> 00:22:42,967
NO!

2581
00:22:42,967 --> 00:22:44,427
Don't be difficult.

2582
00:22:44,427 --> 00:22:46,677
I want to save the <i>NakaMa</i>!

2583
00:22:46,677 --> 00:22:47,637
"<i>NakaMa</i>"?

2584
00:22:47,637 --> 00:22:48,347
Please!

2585
00:22:48,847 --> 00:22:52,057
If we go there, something bad will happen.

2586
00:22:52,057 --> 00:22:53,687
I know it!

2587
00:22:54,187 --> 00:22:56,067
Nothing good will come of it.

2588
00:22:56,857 --> 00:22:58,237
Let's leave them alone!

2589
00:22:58,527 --> 00:23:00,527
Please, Vince?

2590
00:23:00,527 --> 00:23:01,817
Believe me.

2591
00:23:16,757 --> 00:23:18,417
All right then.

2592
00:23:19,507 --> 00:23:20,587
Vince!

2593
00:23:20,587 --> 00:23:21,887
Vincent!

2594
00:23:38,607 --> 00:23:44,657
In this way, Smile Land was saved by a girl.

2595
00:23:45,367 --> 00:23:47,657
Thank you, Smile Girl!

2596
00:23:47,657 --> 00:23:49,577
Thank you, Pino!

